<emu-intro id="sec-introduction">
  <h1>Introduction</h1>
  <p>This working draft exposes ECMA-402 matching for application locales. It specifies no data source or best-fit scoring algorithm. API placement, available-locale extensions, and fallback validation remain open.</p>
</emu-intro>

<emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher">
  <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher</h1>
  <p>The objects and functions defined in this clause are subject to the <a href="https://tc39.es/ecma402/#requirements">requirements for standard built-in ECMAScript objects</a> in ECMA-402.</p>
  <p>The initial value of the *"LocaleMatcher"* property of the Intl object is %Intl.LocaleMatcher%.</p>
  <p>The LocaleMatcher object:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>is an ordinary object.</li>
    <li>has a [[Prototype]] internal slot whose value is %Object.prototype%.</li>
    <li>does not have a [[Call]] internal method.</li>
    <li>does not have a [[Construct]] internal method.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Unless otherwise specified, the properties defined in this clause have the attributes { [[Writable]]: *true*, [[Enumerable]]: *false*, [[Configurable]]: *true* }.</p>

  <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher-tostringtag">
    <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher [ %Symbol.toStringTag% ]</h1>
    <p>The initial value of the %Symbol.toStringTag% property is the String value *"Intl.LocaleMatcher"*.</p>
    <p>This property has the attributes { [[Writable]]: *false*, [[Enumerable]]: *false*, [[Configurable]]: *true* }.</p>
  </emu-clause>

  <emu-clause id="sec-intl.localematcher.match">
    <h1>Intl.LocaleMatcher.match ( _requestedLocales_, _availableLocales_, _defaultLocale_ [ , _options_ ] )</h1>
    <p>This method returns an available locale or the explicit fallback. It performs the following steps when called:</p>
    <emu-alg>
      1. Let _requested_ be ? CanonicalizeLocaleList(_requestedLocales_).
      1. Let _available_ be ? CanonicalizeLocaleList(_availableLocales_).
      1. For each element _locale_ of _available_, do
        1. If _locale_ contains a Unicode locale extension sequence, throw a *RangeError* exception.
      1. Let _fallbackArgument_ be CreateArrayFromList(« _defaultLocale_ »).
      1. Let _fallbackList_ be ? CanonicalizeLocaleList(_fallbackArgument_).
      1. Let _fallback_ be _fallbackList_[0].
      1. Set _options_ to ? GetOptionsObject(_options_).
      1. Let _algorithm_ be ? GetOption(_options_, *"algorithm"*, ~string~, « *"lookup"*, *"best fit"* », *"best fit"*).
      1. If _requested_ is empty or _available_ is empty, return _fallback_.
      1. If _algorithm_ is *"lookup"*, then
        1. Let _match_ be LookupMatchingLocaleByPrefix(_available_, _requested_).
      1. Else,
        1. Let _match_ be LookupMatchingLocaleByBestFit(_available_, _requested_).
      1. If _match_ is *undefined*, return _fallback_.
      1. Return _match_.[[locale]].
    </emu-alg>
    <p>The *"length"* property of this method is *3*<sub>𝔽</sub>.</p>

    <emu-note>
      <p>Available locales describe app resources, independent of Intl service support, host defaults, or parent tags.</p>
      <p>Both lists follow Intl.getCanonicalLocales input semantics, including strings, Intl.Locale objects, and array-like inputs. Sets are not consumed as iterables.</p>
    </emu-note>
    <emu-note>
      <p>Fallback is validated eagerly, may be outside available locales, and does not influence matching. This method does not call DefaultLocale.</p>
    </emu-note>
    <emu-note>
      <p>The result is a canonical available tag or fallback. Requested Unicode locale extensions are not copied; service options are not resolved.</p>
    </emu-note>
    <emu-note>
      <p>Best fit remains implementation-defined. No CLDR/ICU data, scoring, expansion, penalty, or tie policy is required.</p>
      <p>Requested Unicode locale extensions are ignored. Other extensions and private-use subtags follow the selected operation, without assigned application-specific meanings.</p>
    </emu-note>
  </emu-clause>
</emu-clause>
